{
  "_doc": "FACS layer for MotionEngine. au_map: FACS Action Unit -> ARKit base blendshapes (never the TalkingHead composites mouthSmile/mouthOpen/eyesClosed, to avoid double-driving), following the ARKit<->FACS convention and calibrated per-model (e.g. AU12 capped for this over-sculpted mouthSmile). expressions: emotion -> AU recipe + optional envelope. Recipe AU weights are the FINAL levels (one fixed intensity per expression, no runtime scaling): final morph = recipeWeight * au_map weight, clamped 0..1. Unilateral AU via _L/_R suffix (e.g. AU12_L). The 7 'core' recipes use the canonical EMFACS-7 AU combinations; 'extended' recipes are documented blends of the same primitives. aliases resolve free-text emotion words (nouns/verbs/[stage-directions]) to a canonical expression.",
  "_sources": {
    "emfacs": "Emotional FACS (Ekman & Friesen 1983) — canonical AU combinations for the basic emotions. https://www.paulekman.com/facial-action-coding-system/",
    "au_to_arkit": "ARKit<->FACS mapping convention (each ARKit blendshape ~ one FACS AU). https://melindaozel.com/arkit-to-facs-cheat-sheet/ ; clinical blendshape<->AU mapping https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2451958826001995 ; interactive ARKit-52<->AU guide https://arkit.miniface.org/faces",
    "stylized_3d": "AU-Blendshape: Fine-grained Stylized 3D Facial Expression Manipulation (arXiv:2507.12001) — approach for driving stylized (cartoon) 3D faces via Action Units, and the need for per-model AU calibration."
  },
